When demonstrations differ sharply in dimensions, palettes, and object structures, log the exact changed-cell mask and the roles of each color/object separately for every pair. A shared color numeral or visual resemblance is not evidence of a shared transformation. Replay each candidate rule against every complete demo, including untouched cells and identity examples; reject rules that fail any pair. Transfer only a role-level invariant supported across examples. If none is supported, request another demo only when you can name competing hypotheses and the concrete observation that would discriminate them. Avoid speculative large edits based on one salient pattern.

