In a sparse grid, a demo may show a special-color boundary stripe (here, color 9) and isolated markers of another color. The demonstrated changes were limited to horizontal segments: each marker became a distinct leading cell (color 4) followed by a run of marker color (5) through the boundary stripe. The opposite boundary marker extended across its row in the demo. This indicates that output extent and marker treatment are crucial; globally coloring a marker-to-boundary span with the marker's own color, or filling an entire stripe, does not reproduce the pair.

